{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792499123,"nonce":"C/V71fI5NipIvWxwt8NcW0UIdC4=","message":"Final native probes pass after all collector/glass/fallback corrections on Apple M1 Pro / Metal: eight RGBA GPU cases, seven existing composite GPU cases plus its CPU fingerprint case, and four existing motion cases pass in SSBO, forced VB and forced DT. Fallback capacities 1024 with multistop vertex opt-in. Temporary overrides are restored. Existing 45 normal native regressions also pass (producer 2, overlay 7, aux 2, display-list 33, fill-rule 1). Final logs: /private/tmp/blinc-rgba-final-{normal,vb,dt}-app-{rgba,composite,motion}.log plus the final normal regression logs under the same prefix.\n\nThe final canvas test renders three frames through direct and compositor paths, each with and without an actual glass node: two image frames with changed bytes, then shape-only output. It checks group alpha survives image disappearance, image-only callback visit ordering, positive-z translucent single blending and foreground mesh visibility. The public glass-frame fixture also checks foreground and reduced/preserved backdrop dispatch. Actual glass blur/nested-glass pixels are not newly compared to a reference; their existing native sequence is reused. DT preserves ordinary content while unsupported glass is omitted. No glass shader support or border redesign is added.\n\nAll four original CPU/image-order controls and the later transition/foreground/storage-free controls are recorded above with observed failures. Final code retains the explicit render_dynamic_images API, filters already-consumed background records in application late passes, preserves original image/group cursors in the active batch, hashes image bytes/metadata, and requests full paint when primitive-only patchers cannot represent images. It does not complete foreground RGBA grouping, separate text/SVG/ImageElement isolation, cross-stream ancestor isolation, arbitrary image affine transforms or non-rectangular clipping. Both parent issues remain open. Browser/mobile pixels, timings and memory benchmarks are unverified. Nothing pushed.","files":null}]}